Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 05:41:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Restore the selected disc when loading a state

Loading a state restored the CD-ROM image but left the frontend's
selected index unchanged. An M3U state also stored only the playlist
path and subimage number, so changing the playlist could select a
different disc.

Add a small trailer with the selected path and tray state. Match the
path against the current list before loading, using a unique filename
match for moved images. Reject missing or ambiguous entries instead
of leaving the callbacks and mounted media pointing at different
discs. The existing machine payload stays compatible with old states.

Tested all six Metal Gear Solid disc/tray combinations, loading after
playlist edits, moved images and malformed states. Old M3U states
still load; their numeric indices cannot identify a playlist that was
reordered on disk before the state was opened.
